From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 07 Oct 2026 10:58:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: fix use-after-free in mt7915_mac_sta_rc_work

The rate control work takes a station off the list under
sta_poll_lock, drops the lock, and then sends MCU commands for the
station, which sleep. The work does not hold the device mutex. If the
station is removed in that window, the driver removal callback finds
the entry already off the list and does not wait, and mac80211 frees
the station while the work still uses it.

Hold the device mutex for the whole work, as e2a5529fa153 ("wifi:
mt76: mt7996: Add missing locking in mt7996_mac_sta_rc_work()") does
for mt7996. Station removal holds the same mutex, so every station on
the list stays valid until the work is done with it.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7915/mac.c |    7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -1954,6 +1954,11 @@ void mt7915_mac_sta_rc_work(struct work_
 	u32 changed;
 	LIST_HEAD(list);
 
+	/* Station removal holds this mutex, so a station on the list stays
+	 * valid while the MCU commands below sleep.
+	 */
+	mutex_lock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
+
 	spin_lock_bh(&dev->mt76.sta_poll_lock);
 	list_splice_init(&dev->sta_rc_list, &list);
 
@@ -1979,6 +1984,8 @@ void mt7915_mac_sta_rc_work(struct work_
 	}
 
 	spin_unlock_bh(&dev->mt76.sta_poll_lock);
+
+	mutex_unlock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
 }
 
 static void mt7915_mac_adm_count_clear(struct mt7915_dev *dev)
